<span id="Description"></span>
==Beschreibung==

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The [[Image:Part_LinkArrayCircular.svg|24px]] '''Part LinkArrayCircular''' command creates a [[App_Link|Link]] array from a selected object by placing copies along concentric circles.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The command can be used on many 3D objects such as those created with the [[Part_Workbench|Part Workbench]], but also on assembly instances created with the [[Assembly_Workbench|Assembly Workbench]].
</div>

<span id="Usage"></span>
==Anwendung==

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
# Optionally select one object.
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Part_LinkArrayCircular.svg|16px]] [[Part_LinkArrayCircular|Circular Link Array]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part/Assembly → Link Arrays → [[Image:Part_LinkArrayCircular.svg|16px]] Circular Link Array}} option from the menu.
# The {{MenuCommand|Circular Link Array}} task panel opens. See [[#Options|Options]] for more information.
# If you have not yet selected an object, press the {{Button|Select Object}} button and select one object.
# Enter the required parameters in the task panel.
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button to finish the command.
</div>

<span id="Options"></span>
==Optionen==

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Select the {{MenuCommand|Axis}} to specify the axis about which the array will be created. It can be X-, Y- or Z-axis, or a selected reference.
* Enter the {{MenuCommand|Radial distance}} to specify the radial distance between the circular layers. Must be larger than zero.
* Enter the {{MenuCommand|Tangential distance}} to specify the tangential distance between the elements in the circular layers. Must be larger than zero.
* Enter the number of {{MenuCommand|Concentric circles}}. The element at the center counts as one circle. Must be at least {{Value|2}}.
* Enter the {{MenuCommand|Symmetry}} value. This number determines how the elements are distributed. A value of {{Value|3}}, for example, results in a pattern with three equal 120° pie segments. Larger values for the {{MenuCommand|Symmetry}} and the {{MenuCommand|Tangential distance}} result in fewer or even no elements on the inner layers.
* Press the {{Button|Cancel}} button to abort the command.
</div>


